course: dictionary
lesson: 15948
title: Unsound: not safe, not reliable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unsound means not safe or strong, or in bad condition. An unsound bridge might fall down, so people must not cross it. Unsound can also describe ideas. Unsound reasoning is based on wrong facts or poor thinking, so it cannot be trusted.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The old bridge was unsound, so the council closed it.» The closing tells you the bridge was dangerous, so unsound means not safe to use. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: «Her argument was unsound, because one of her facts was wrong.» Argument is about ideas, so unsound here means not based on good sense or facts. The word tells the reader: do not trust this.
fact: Unsound means not safe or strong, or in bad condition.
fact: «Unsound» can describe a building, a bridge, ice, or a shelf that might break.
fact: For ideas, unsound means based on wrong facts or poor thinking, so it is unreliable.
fact: The opposite of unsound is sound: a sound bridge is safe, and a sound argument is based on good facts.
fact: In an old law phrase, «of unsound mind» meant a person was seriously mentally ill and could not make responsible decisions.
exercise: «The old bridge was unsound, so the council closed it.» What does unsound mean here? | *Not safe to use | Full of happy people | Freshly painted | Very long and wide
exercise: «Her argument was unsound, because one of her facts was wrong.» Ruby says unsound means loud. What does it mean? | Made of sound | Sung in a choir | *Not based on good sense or facts | Very loud
exercise: «The shelf was unsound, so do not stand on it.» Find and copy the word that tells you the shelf is not safe. | *unsound | do | stand | shelf
test: «The ice looked thick, but it was unsound.» What does this tell you? | It is melting slowly in the sun | It is perfect for skating | *It may break under you, so keep off | It is a new kind of snow
test: Which sentence shows unsound reasoning? | Penguins are birds, and birds have wings, so penguins have wings | *All birds fly, penguins are birds, so penguins fly | Cats have fur, and my cat has fur, so my cat has fur | Ice melts when it is warm, so ice in the sun will melt
exam: «The tree looked healthy, but its roots were rotten and unsound.» What does unsound mean? | Strong and safe | Sung loudly | Very healthy and green | *Not safe or strong, in bad condition
